DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggvviinnuumm utility communicates with the kernel component of the GVinum
     logical volume manager.  It is designed either for interactive use, when
     started without command line arguments, or to execute a single command if
     the command is supplied on the command line.  In interactive mode, ggvviinnuumm
     maintains a command line history.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     The ggvviinnuumm commands may be followed by an option.

     --ff      The --ff (“force”) option overrides safety checks.  It should be
             used with extreme caution.  This option is required in order to
             use the mmoovvee command.

     --rr      The --rr (“recursive”) option applies the command recursively to
             subordinate objects.  For example, in conjunction with the llvv
             command, the --rr option will also show information about the
             plexes and subdisks belonging to the volume.  It is also used by
             the rreennaammee command to indicate that subordinate objects such as
             subdisks should be renamed to match the object(s) specified and
             by the rrmm command to delete plexes belonging to a volume and so
             on.

     --vv      The --vv (“verbose”) option provides more detailed output.

     --VV      The --VV (“very verbose”) option provides even more detailed output
             than --vv.

