BBUUGGSS
     Currently, ggvviinnuumm does not rename devices in _/_d_e_v_/_g_v_i_n_u_m until reloaded.

     The --SS initsize flag to ssttaarrtt is ignored.

     Moving subdisks that are not part of a mirrored or RAID-5 volume will de‐
     stroy data.  It is perhaps a bug to permit this.

     Plexes in which subdisks have been moved do not automatically sync or re‐
     build parity.  This may leave data unprotected and is perhaps unwise.

     Currently, ggvviinnuumm does not yet fully implement all of the functions found
     in vviinnuumm.  Specifically, the following commands from vviinnuumm are not sup‐
     ported:

     ddeebbuugg   Cause the volume manager to enter the kernel debugger.

